Both mandated cross-host pairs are implemented, verified, and green.

## What was built

**`test/yin/repl/slice_peer.clj` → `slice_peer.cljc`** — the peer is now one portable program in two roles, host-conditional with `:cljd` branches first throughout:
- *Client role* (no args): the same pipe protocol as round 1, now on JVM/Node/Dart (per-host stdin/stdout/ticker idioms mirror `dao.stream.slice-peer`).
- *Server role* (`--serve <host> <port>`): a real headless endpoint — `serve!` + one ticker, `Serving …` as the parent's readiness signal, `{:cmd :stop}` as the stop trigger, stepping to `:stopped` before exit.

**Pair 1 — cljd client vs JVM server** (`a-dart-client-attaches-to-this-jvm-server`, clj block of `v2_test.cljc`): reuses the fixture endpoint, spawns the Dart exe, and proves connect, the `(+ 40 2)` → `42` round trip, the **outstanding-request-lost report** across the wire, the Dart attachment handle answering `:dao.stream/closed`, and the JVM boundary depositing the departure.

**Pair 2 — Node client vs cljd server** (`a-node-client-attaches-to-a-dart-server`, new cljs block): spawns the Dart `--serve` peer; the Node test process itself is the client (`repl/boot` + one interval step owner, exactly the real Node host composition). Asserts connect, the `42` round trip, then `:stop` → the client observes **`:ended`, not a detach** — the ended-stream close-code semantics cross the wire. A bonus JVM-client↔Dart-server pairing was verified ad hoc during development.

**`bb.edn`**: new `build:yin-repl-peer` (cljd compile + `dart compile exe`); `test:cljd` restructured to `:depends [build:slice-peer build:yin-repl-peer]`; aggregate `test` builds the peer first so the full pipeline always exercises the cross pairs. **`shadow-cljs.edn`: no change needed** (the Node side is an in-process client; the Dart exe covers both child roles) — the authorization went unused.

## A real bug found and fixed along the way

Stability-looping the namespace exposed a ~1-in-6 flake: the peer's `:events` handler drained its publication atom with deref-then-reset, racing the ticker — events (e.g. `Connected to …`) could be **cleared without ever being sent**, with no error anywhere. Diagnosis took a probe/trace instrumentation pass (lifecycle cursor at position 1, status `:established`, event never delivered); the fix is an atomic `compare-and-set!` take. The instrumented `:probe`/`:trace` remain in the peer as documented read-only diagnostics. Two assertion bugs of my own were also fixed: substring matching on answers (`"42"` matches a port like `…:42999/repl`) now uses exact equality on both clj and cljs sides.

